In article <19466@helios.TAMU.EDU> z0w3116@summa.tamu.edu writes:
>My wizard lost the telepathy intrinsic right before the Medusa level. I wonder
>when this losing intrinsic happens? I don't remember attacking any friendly
>monster, but he did fight a lich. Does the lich's spell take intrinsic?

No.  Could be a gremlin attack, or you killed a priest(ess) etc.  I remember
reading that someone died from loosing fire restiance thanks to a new (wo)man
polymorph, so it might be possible to loose intrinsics that way as well.

>So you never put on ring of levitation when you are in hell, right?

I always do, but being chaotic makes it lots safer.  Also, I usually keep
holy water in either a bag of holding or a sack for uncursing my ring, blind-
fold, or unicorn horn.

>One more: What is the use of gauntlet of dexterity? A +0 gauntlet of dexterity
>does not increase your dexterity. Does it increase your speed? But I see no
>difference after putting it on. Maybe it doesn't accumulate with speed boots?

Gauntlets of dexterity increase your dex, not your speed.  They increase your
dexterity according to their enchantment, so a +0 pair yields no benefit (or
detriment) to your dexterity.
